BTC TRADING APPLICATION — INSTITUTIONAL ARCHITECT REVIEW
Classification: Internal Audit | Date: 2026-06-01 (Updated) | Original: 2026-05-31 | Panel: Principal Quant, HFT Infra, Security, Risk, DB, Go, Next.js, Systems Architect
Last update reflects Phase 11–14 additions: microstructure alpha engine, OMS v3, ledger, kill switch, reconciliation, performance layer, ML classifier, Redis caching, TimescaleDB schema, and full observability stack.

EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
This platform is a sophisticated multi-market algorithmic trading system with genuine architectural ambition. The research tournament, multi-model AI consensus, and 100+ strategy registry demonstrate real engineering depth. Since the initial audit, Phases 11–14 have addressed the majority of the critical alpha gaps identified in the BTC Alpha Review (Phase 4): CVD divergence, funding rate engine, liquidity sweep reversal, volume profile, fair value gaps, liquidation cascade, market structure shift, and order block detection are all now implemented under engine/internal/alpha/. The ML classifier (engine/internal/ml/) has been added as a replacement path for the LLM council latency ceiling. A new OMS v3, kill switch, ledger, reconciliation service, and performance/telemetry layer have been added.

The platform is approaching production readiness. Critical security blockers (exposed credentials, unauthenticated endpoints) remain the primary live-deployment risk. With 2–4 weeks of security hardening and integration testing of the new modules, the system is credible for live trading at small scale.

